diff --git a/docs/spec/m17.md b/docs/spec/m17.md
index 86a95a7..189990c 100644
--- a/docs/spec/m17.md
+++ b/docs/spec/m17.md
@@ -113,7 +113,7 @@ frame; playback starts with four frames queued. With no encoder frame ready the
 | Memory | none of its own where the vocoder lends its code window (`hal_vocoder_t.lend_window`, `HAL_VOCODER_WINDOW`: the HR_C7000 platform, 83,456 B, idle while no DMR voice runs). While M17 runs the window holds the engine (about 1.8 KB), Codec 2's state and FFT tables (31,392 B on a 64-bit host, in a 31,744 B arena, `M17_VOICE_ARENA`) and the codec's stack. The vocoder's calls give silence meanwhile; leaving M17 copies its code back from the slot. Without a lending vocoder (the host tests) a static block holds the engine and the arena |
 | Stack | Codec 2 runs on its own 24 KB (`M17_VOICE_STACK`) at the top of the window, through `hal_vocoder_t.call_on_stack` (`platform/hrc7000/call_on_stack.S`), not on the audio task's: 17,832 B used on a 64-bit host (m17VoiceTest runs it on such a stack). The audio task's stack and the FreeRTOS heap are unchanged |
 | CPU | `CODEC2_FIXED_3200` replaces the floating-point 3200 encoder with an integer TX analysis path (Q20 LPC/LSP, integer pitch, energy and LSPD quantization). It emits standard 64-bit Codec 2 3200 frames and has no floating-point/libm dependency in its host object; it is not bit-exact with upstream, especially in pitch and voicing. The reference floating-point decoder remains for RX and interoperability. The original encoder/decoder cost counted on CK803S code was 19.2/20.1 million instructions per 20 ms (114/120 ms at 168 MHz even at one instruction per cycle), and codec creation was 22.9 million; those counts do not measure the new fixed TX path. Host `m17VoiceTest` measured at most 12 us inside fixed encode and 34 us inside reference decode on the test machine; these are not CK803S timings |
-| Too slow | Each encode and decode is timed on the provider's microsecond clock. One over 15 ms (`M17_VOICE_BUDGET_US`) switches the codec off until a restart (`m17VoiceSlow`): no more codec calls, so the audio task, which runs above the radio and UI tasks, no longer keeps them out (before this check a slow codec held it busy without end: the radio froze on PTT). A transmission is cut and unkeyed, PTT refused (`TXDENY_CPU`, "CPU too slow for voice", with "M17 enc X dec Y ms"), received calls stay silent; the call's fields still show. The home screen's chips line shows the times in place of the CAN, the TX screen after the CAN. The fixed TX path does not disable or relax this protection |
+| Too slow | Codec 2 blocks budget 18 ms against the 20 ms PCM cadence. Faster blocks repay accumulated lag. At 20 ms of lag, RX mutes the current call and TX cuts and unkeys with `TXDENY_CPU` ("CPU too slow for voice"). The next call can retry. The chips and TX screens show the maximum encode and decode times. |
 
